From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tarikbc <tarikbc@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:07:39 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] ARM64EC: fix the NtDllRedirectionLUT size load and bounds check in
 CheckCall

NtDllRedirectionLUTSize is a uint32_t; a 64-bit ldr only links while it happens to be
8-byte aligned, and the globals added by the next patch move it. The bounds check used
b.hi, which let an offset equal to the size through and read one entry past the end of
the LUT.

Upstream: both commits of FEX-Emu/FEX#6021 (4dbb046d62, 3a2b1c0b43; merged as 94ff2b0c6,
2026-10-12). Drop this patch at FEX-2611.
---
 Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.S | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.S b/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.S
index 2489e653c..ce36c1d68 100644
--- a/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.S
+++ b/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.S
@@ -158,9 +158,9 @@ DIRECT_SYSCALL_WRAPPER("#NtProtectVirtualMemoryNative", WineNtProtectVirtualMemo
   subs x16, x11, x9
   b.lo end
   adrp x17, NtDllRedirectionLUTSize
-  ldr x17, [x17, #:lo12:NtDllRedirectionLUTSize]
+  ldr w17, [x17, #:lo12:NtDllRedirectionLUTSize]
   cmp x16, x17
-  b.hi end
+  b.hs end
   adrp x17, NtDllRedirectionLUT
   ldr x17, [x17, #:lo12:NtDllRedirectionLUT]
   ldr w11, [x17, x16, lsl #2]
